{"id":"s5.1.1","slug":"systems-of-equations","title":"Systems of Two Linear Equations","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Number sense systems are built to collapse in one step. Look first for a variable whose coefficients are equal and opposite — adding the equations eliminates it immediately.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For $ax + by = c$ and $dx - by = e$, adding gives $(a+d)x = c + e$, so $x = \\frac{c+e}{a+d}$. Substitute back only if the question asks for the other variable.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">If neither variable cancels directly, check whether one equation is a small multiple of the other before doing any real work.</p>","summary":"Number sense systems are built to collapse in one step.","generation_guideline":"Generate a 2x2 linear system whose solution is a small rational number.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Let $8x + 1y = 70$ and $7x - 1y = 50$. Find $x$.","answer":"8","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":2,"text":"Let $9x + 4y = -3$ and $2x - 4y = 14$. Find $x$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":3,"text":"Let $3x + 3y = 33$ and $2x - 3y = -8$. Find $x$.","answer":"5","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":4,"text":"Let $4x + 3y = 25$ and $2x - 3y = -1$. Find $x$.","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":5,"text":"Let $2x + 4y = -8$ and $2x - 4y = 40$. Find $x$.","answer":"8","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":6,"text":"Let $6x + 6y = -6$ and $4x - 6y = -54$. Find $x$.","answer":"-6","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":7,"text":"Let $7x + 5y = -44$ and $6x - 5y = 18$. Find $y$.","answer":"-6","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":8,"text":"Let $3x + 1y = 17$ and $2x - 1y = 3$. Find $y$.","answer":"5","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":9,"text":"Let $7x + 6y = -6$ and $2x - 6y = -48$. Find $y$.","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":10,"text":"Let $9x + 4y = 42$ and $6x - 4y = 48$. Find $x$.","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":11,"text":"Let $5x + 5y = 45$ and $7x - 5y = -3